cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Seabraid: an engine-neutral runtime for same-layer mixed-vendor Mixture-of-Experts execution"
type: software
version: 0.5.0-alpha.8
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/saltwater-research/seabraid"
authors:
  - name: "Saltwater Research LLC"
    email: "dev@saltyresearch.com"
abstract: >-
  Seabraid lets GPUs from different vendors (NVIDIA CUDA and AMD ROCm) serve the
  experts of one Mixture-of-Experts model at the same layer. Each card runs
  vendor-native kernels in its own process; the processes meet in shared
  memory once per layer. The runtime provides an engine-neutral C ABI and
  acknowledged live expert placement.
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - inference
  - heterogeneous GPUs
  - expert placement
  - CUDA
  - ROCm
